// Measure then read, the third of the paper's three opening programs, in its
// attempted spelling: measure the temporary, keep the post-measurement
// register, read it into the visible register, then drop it.  Silq's measure
// consumes its argument, so this program names the temporary after measuring
// it, which is the point being tested.
def main(){
	t := H(0:𝔹);
	p := measure(t);
	x := 0:𝔹;
	if t { x := X(x); }   // use t AFTER measuring it
	forget(t);
	return measure(x);
}
